  "num_turns": null,
  "final_message": "I fixed the bug in `add_tag`, and `python3 -m unittest -v test_public.py` now passes (1 test).\n\n**The bug:** the default `tags=[]` is created once, when the function is defined, and then shared by every call that leaves `tags` out. So tags from one call leaked into the next.\n\n**The fix:** the default is now `None`, and the function creates a new empty list whenever `tags` isn't passed.\n\nIf you do pass your own list, `add_tag` still appends to that same list in place. I checked this: the record ends up holding your list itself, not a copy. `remove_tag` is unchanged.\n\nDONE: Replaced the mutable default `tags=[]` in `add_tag` with `tags=None` plus a new empty list per call; a list you pass in is still used as given, and the public test passes.",
